WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.160
- [Voiceover] In 1992,
the Japanese government

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.240
introduced strict new laws against Japan's

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.160
organized crime syndicates, the Yakuza,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.440
in order to undermine their,
at that point in time,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.920
substantial power.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.880
(laughing)

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.200
Once an army of more than 80,000,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.960
their numbers are the lowest since 1992.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.240
And the traditional world of the Yakuza,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.880
which has been existing
since the 17th century,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.960
is crumbling.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.480
- [Voiceover] To this date,
Japan has one of the lowest

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.720
crime rates in the industrial world.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.000
With crimes related to
drugs being strikingly low.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.640
A fact many contribute to the
very existence of the Yakuza,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.400
Japan's so called necessary evil.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.760
- Good morning.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.080
Have a nice day.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.840
Good morning!

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.640
Banzai, banzai, banzai!

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.520
Lucky!

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.760
Go, go, go, go!

00:45:32.400 --> 00:45:36.160
(traditional Japanese music)

00:55:54.920 --> 00:55:57.240
(gun shots)

00:56:04.080 --> 00:56:06.400
(gun shots)

00:59:44.880 --> 00:59:47.800
25 years to professional wrestling.

01:04:55.000 --> 01:04:55.920
Okay, okay!

01:08:06.160 --> 01:08:09.240
(Japanese pop music)

01:44:45.360 --> 01:44:47.160
- Hello, how are you?

01:44:47.160 --> 01:44:48.600
- I am very fine.

